    "body": "**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\r\nEE mostly uses session based cookies, but sets a number of \"Strictly Necessary\" cookies that are \"persistent\" beyond the session.  These are flash (1 day), last_activity (1 year), last_visit (1 year), remember (2 weeks),  visitor_consents (1 year).\r\n\r\nThe presence of these persistent cookies trips a wire in GDPR - for each of these cookies it is necessary for the developer to provide justification for the need for the persistent cookie and report that the cookie cannot be linked to user activity.  Sometimes these justifications are not heard sympathetically - if the 'strictly necessary' determination is not accepted then these cookies must only be set if a visitor to the site from a GDPR country actively consents.\r\n\r\nThere is no mechanism in EE either to adjust the duration of these cookies, or to link their creation to active consent.\r\n\r\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\r\nAn option in EE CP to set the duration of all cookies to be session based by default.\r\n\r\nIf there are functional benefits to be gained by making any of the cookies have a longer life, this should be a choice that can be made by users and set using the consent features of EE.\r\n\r\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\r\nThere are no alternative solutions right now.\r\n\r\n**Teachability, Documentation, Adoption, Migration Strategy**\r\nHow this gets documented depends on the solution that is adopted.\r\nProvided switching to session duration cookies is not something that breaks EE, there should be no migration issues.\r\n",
